{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri","id":1487957,"title":"Remaking the Salubri","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-25T18:11:43-07:00","id":1487957,"title":"Remaking the Salubri","content":"What the title says.<br /> <br /> You have a task of making the Salubri for your favorite edition of V:TM!<br /> <br /> How would you redo them!<br /> <br /> What sparks the changes in-universe, if anything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T18:13:38-07:00","id":1487958,"title":"","content":"REPOST:<br /> <br /> I once did some notes up for Healer Salubri that were able to survive in Africa, the Middle East, and Asia that the Tremere eventually had to realize that they were never going to be able to deal with for a &quot;Global Camarilla&quot; campaign I had. The rub being the Tremere discovered most of them gave absolutely no shits about the diablerie of Saulot and were powerful enough the Tremere had to make peace with.<br /> <br /> The interpretation I went with was admittedy much darker but not ditching the concept entirely. The idea of trying to make a Clan of Salubri that has the same basic concept but dark enough to fit with the other Clans as well as a game of personal horror.<br /> <br /> Here's my notes:<br /> <br /> * The Salubri Clan weakness remained being unable to feed from unwilling vessels. Unwilling being defined as those not entranced, involuntarily there, or otherwise resisting. They are masters of loophole abuse on this.<br /> * The Salubri Embrace doctors, morticians, hospice owners, religious leaders, and people involved in the medical trade.<br /> * Lots of people do die because of the Salubri influence but they try to minimize their &quot;vampire footprint.&quot;<br /> * They are heavily involved in the local blood trades and frequently pass off spikes in deaths as the result of disease outbreaks.<br /> * Salubri have their own Roads that have survived since the Dark Ages that basically amount to &quot;God said it was okay to feed on you&quot; and &quot;Feeding from the already dying and elderly is fine.&quot;<br /> * Some Salubri blood bond people they consider undesirable and keep herds that are left to lose ghouldom but not their devotion. These people are willing vessels they feed on over the course of years until death.<br /> * Other vampires consider Salubri less saints and more, &quot;Hospital feeders.&quot;<br /> * Local variants of the Salubri included Animalism and Presence to go with Obeah because these allow a lot more feeding alternatives.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T19:21:46-07:00","id":1487966,"title":"","content":"I would do a heavy overhaul with them, but it is almost entirely fluff and lore reworks, rather than mechanics.<br /> <br /> Make them a Camarilla clan, with the Healers being numerous, and the Warriors being the fabled low generation group who act as watch dogs for the return of the Baali. If nothing else, it would smooth out the Camarillas stewardship of mortals and help cement the pro humanity path ideal.<br /> <br /> Considering the long history of problems between the Brujah and Ventrue, yet they can still be factional allies, the Salubri and Tremere wouldn't be that big of an issue work on the same side. Just rework the Salubri purge narrative from the fluff and have them purge the Warrior branch of the line due to some leftover demonic taint from the Baali wars. Yeah the Salubri are going to be cranky at the Tremere for purging a portion of the clan and eating their founder, but that is only in the last 500 years, where as the Brujah/Ventrue feud is millennia long at this point.<br /> <br /> The Salubri Healers are still a hard mode play style due to their feeding restrictions and low initial combat potential, which retains their feel but it makes more sense from a setting perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T20:05:48-07:00","id":1487968,"title":"","content":"Can't post a full thing ATM but I would have had them in both the Vampire the Dark Ages and Dark Ages Vampire core books as if they were still a full clan, even if their founder is apparently gone and we know OOC that they are doomed. And in DAV, they'd be fully integrated into the High Clans and their society/power structure, as well as prevalent among the followers of all the Roads, especially of Humanity, Heaven, and Sin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T21:32:47-07:00","id":1487975,"title":"","content":"I'd pretty much ignore the purge to begin with, it is wholly unnecessary for this. There was a conflict where the Tremere Diablerized a lot of their elders, but a full blown persecution simply isn't necessary. Before the Camarilla the Salubri simply couldn't politically stand to the Prestation machine of the Tremere and after, if the Gangrel and Nosferatu could agree to end hostilities with the Warlocks in exchange for a peace treaty, why wouldn't the Salubri? I also personally find any clan whatsoever being attached to crimes against half-forgotten elders a ludicrous idea.<br /> <br /> Warrior Salubri are rare and extremely careful to Embrace as they were in the Dark Ages. Many act as enforcers or on military roles of some kind for the Camarilla. Healers are the bulk of the clan and somehow compensate greater numbers and political presence with the expected lessened demand on moral compliance. They offer the benefits of Obeah in a similar way the Tremere offer magic, sometimes with competition arising, others with both clans reaching a profitable partnership.<br /> <br /> One thing I would borrow from the Wu-Zao is the ability to switch Castes: with help of a member from the other caste, a Salubri can go through a process that change their Discipline between Obeah and Valeren (even if they have it at 0 dots). Some few can even chose to Embrace into the other caste instead of their own, although this is a rare ability, rarer still to be used, but not unheard of.<br /> <br /> Healers that want to become Warriors must go through rigorous selection as if it was for the Embrace, or present proof of dire need for such change. On the other hand, Healers accept to turn Warriors with ease, frequently receiving among them those Warriors that failed the high standards of their peers. Sometimes this is used so the Warriors can muster higher numbers for a coming battle, dismissing the extra hands after as Healers, the &quot;Veterans&quot;.<br /> <br /> And finally, if there is a member of the clan among the Inner Circle, at this point I would just put Saulot himself there. If there's one Ante to whom the position fits, it's him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T21:43:09-07:00","id":1487976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1487958#post1487958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> REPOST:<br /> <br /> I once did some notes up for Healer Salubri that were able to survive in Africa, the Middle East, and Asia that the Tremere eventually had to realize that they were never going to be able to deal with for a &quot;Global Camarilla&quot; campaign I had. The rub being the Tremere discovered most of them gave absolutely no shits about the diablerie of Saulot and were powerful enough the Tremere had to make peace with.<br /> <br /> The interpretation I went with was admittedy much darker but not ditching the concept entirely. The idea of trying to make a Clan of Salubri that has the same basic concept but dark enough to fit with the other Clans as well as a game of personal horror.<br /> <br /> Here's my notes:<br /> <br /> * The Salubri Clan weakness remained being unable to feed from unwilling vessels. Unwilling being defined as those not entranced, involuntarily there, or otherwise resisting. They are masters of loophole abuse on this.<br /> * The Salubri Embrace doctors, morticians, hospice owners, religious leaders, and people involved in the medical trade.<br /> * Lots of people do die because of the Salubri influence but they try to minimize their &quot;vampire footprint.&quot;<br /> * They are heavily involved in the local blood trades and frequently pass off spikes in deaths as the result of disease outbreaks.<br /> * Salubri have their own Roads that have survived since the Dark Ages that basically amount to &quot;God said it was okay to feed on you&quot; and &quot;Feeding from the already dying and elderly is fine.&quot;<br /> * Some Salubri blood bond people they consider undesirable and keep herds that are left to lose ghouldom but not their devotion. These people are willing vessels they feed on over the course of years until death.<br /> * Other vampires consider Salubri less saints and more, &quot;Hospital feeders.&quot;<br /> * Local variants of the Salubri included Animalism and Presence to go with Obeah because these allow a lot more feeding alternatives.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you did a pretty good job. If it was me, I would just give them a brand new blood magic tradition, and say that its used to help them achieve spiritual enlithenment, or something. Make it a mixture of sadhana, assamite sorcery, and perhaps a bit of koldunic sorcery, some real spiritual stuff. I was planning on making something similar to this, but havent found the time to do so yet, for fun of course.<br /> <br /> For the Salubri purge I would probably have tremere hunt down and kill the ones that perferred martial prowess over mystical might, so similir to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar727_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"727\" data-vbnamecard=\"727\">Thoth</a> said just kill of the warrior bloodline or have them join the sabbat. The ones that were more involved in their magical studies always stuck together and were largely left untouched because they either retreated into the umbra, or similarly to the Kolduns, they had power over the spirits of the land making them largely untouchable.<br /> <br /> I would probably change their weakness to having an aura of otherworldliness. Perhaps Saluot was so entrenced in his studies of spirits and the umbra, that whenever he came back from his regular jaunts to the umbra, a piece of it would stick with him, and later affect his decendants. Anyone that is in close proximity to a Salubri, would immediately feel the pull of something otherworldy and immediately turn to the salubri in question. I would have it where people and animals would stop what they were doing and stare uncontrollably. Those in cars would loose focus and crash into each other, birds and insects dropping to the concrete. But they would never stop staring. As you can see, this would be a huge masquerade breach.<br /> <br /> Salubri wasn't diablerized, Tremere failed and ran way, and instead decided to create a ritual that would lower his generation at the cost of permanently weakening his will, and decreasing his mental aptitude. The Tremere clan keeps that under wraps, and claims that Saluot escaped. The salubri could care less about what the warlocks claim.<br /> <br /> Remove the third eye, and make them a bit more apathetic, not emotionless like true brujah, but less focused on the material and more on the immaterial. I would also have the Salubri be more dissapointed in the Tremere than angry. The warlocks have all the time and power in the world to uncover mysteries of the cosmos, and they instead choose to focus their magic on manipulating the physical world, and playing politics, than understanding the spiritual world. The salubri would see it as a waste of talent and resources more than anything else. They would of course not wish to talk about their warrior brethren as they see them as the failures of the clan for not engaging in at least some academic study of the spirits, their curse could just stay the same. So it would be fitting that the warriors would join the sabbat. The main body of the clan would rather stay independant, to continue their studies.<br /> <br /> Of course in this version they would be viewed as something alien, and probably best left alone by other vampires.<br /> <br /> Honetly, your version is seems more thought out so it may be best to stick with that. My version probably delves deeper into the the supernatural side of vtm, than the political.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-26-2022, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T22:06:02-07:00","id":1487979,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about this but I've played around with the idea that the <b>Children of Osiris</b> are actually a Salubri blood cult.<br /> <br /> In this version, <b>Osiris</b> was a Salubri Methuselah of the 4th generation Embraced by Saulot and had a number of progeny before he was killed for a second time. The Salubri of Egypt have since been hiding their Bloodline ever since and the reason that they have been recruiting other vampires into their ranks than Embracing others is they really didn't want to clue in the Tremere about their existence as well as double their enemies.<br /> <br /> The 5th generation and below Bardo users (which is just an Amalgam or variant power of Obeah) are still Salubri protected by the Ashirra and Laibon but they are keeping it on the down low because they could rebuild their Clan pretty easily if they weren't being hunted. They might have other Salubri &quot;hiding in plain sight&quot; among the Osirians or in torpor waiting for the situation to change.<br /> <br /> With the Ministry splitting the Setites in half and the destruction of Vienna, now might be the time for the Children of Osiris Blood Cult to reveal the Salubri were never away at all. Mind you, quite a few older vampires probably have a bone to pick with them over their warrior's occasional vampire hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-26-2022, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T04:32:17-07:00","id":1488004,"title":"","content":"-Salubri have no problem hiding that they're Salubri. The eye only needs to appear when they use their signature discipline. <br /> -The Healer bloodline who were so nice that they needed people's consent to feed is anti-Tremere propaganda. <br /> -The Warrior bloodline are very prominent in the Sabbat. Not in the top 3, but on the level of a clan rather than a bloodline. <br /> -The Seven, though I've never used them, should be kept mysterious to give the Storyteller the maximum amount of leeway. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Other ideas I had floating around: <br /> The Salubri should originally have a lot of Thaumaturges among their number, perhaps giving the Tremere a more solid reason to target them. <br /> I like the old Diamonion/Valaren 6+ connection, though I have no strong opinions on whether this should be accident or a result of shared ancestry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T06:53:01-07:00","id":1488016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1487966#post1487966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would do a heavy overhaul with them, but it is almost entirely fluff and lore reworks, rather than mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is mostly where I am, thought I like CTPhipps list as well. I would have the Salubri include a lot of combat medics, ER staff, and therapists as well. I would utterly do away with the entire \u201cthere are only seven of them and they have childre diablerize their sires\u201d thing as it is odd and very limiting. I would not have them in the Cam, but a free clan like the Ravi\u2019s, or once upon a time the Giovanni and the Settites. They could be difficult to deal with, but weren\u2019t feared. <br /> <br /> And most secretly doubled as vampire hunters. Thought that was not widely known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T07:22:30-07:00","id":1488018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1488004#post1488004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Salubri have no problem hiding that they're Salubri. The eye only needs to appear when they use their signature discipline.<br /> -The Healer bloodline who were so nice that they needed people's consent to feed is anti-Tremere propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would their weakness be, then?<br /> <br /> I personally think those are actually both good options for we to chose, but not to keep both. The feeding restriction isn't necessarily a sign they are too nice, it is just a feeding restriction not unlike what the Ventrue have. And just like the Ventrue, I think it is interesting as a way to give a solid basis for general clan behavior: not all Salubri follow clan culture to any degree, but even those have to deal with the need for &quot;non-resistance&quot; from their vessels. But then I would agree to drop the whole Obligatory Third Eye thing unless using their clan Discipline (and make it subtle even when using most of its powers).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, having the Third Eye all the time could be the Weakness itself. It could bring some inconveniences since an extra eye may mess with perception or be too sensible even when hidden, or just hard to hide, while visible it would be obviously unnatural as it is a moving eye. The simplest solution I can think of is that covering the eye would give you a -1 dice penalty (+1 dif may be too much) on actions that require sight (most of them), as having to work with one of your functioning eyes blocked is just annoying (maybe more than normal with this one). The penalty increases of the cover isn't soft enough (it's a very sensible eye, not a hard patch of skin).<br /> <br /> Personally I find the <i>Antitribu</i> weakness plainly stupid. They could get either of those or something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T07:31:55-07:00","id":1488021,"title":"","content":"If I were to rewrite the Salubri I'd probably have the Salubri split between all of the factions. At this point there isn't really a clan or anti-clan, the clan itself is completely split with the Healers in the Camarilla, Warriors in the Sabbat and Watchers operating as independents or in the Anarchs in 5e. Of course, you'd still have members of the various bloodlines in every faction, but they'd be in the minority.<br /> <br /> Most of the Warriors ended up joining the Sabbat in order to survive the Tremere purge and they hate the Tremere and the Camarilla. About 250 years ago the Healers ended up coming to a peace agreement with the Tremere and joined the Camarilla. They've mostly forgiven the Tremere, or at least they're willing to paper over the past. They don't really get along with the Tremere, and there's still some bad blood, but for the most part, what's in the past is in the past. The Warriors have not forgiven the Tremere, and as a result the Warriors think of the Healers as traitors who have turned their backs on their brothers who were slaughtered by the Tremere. Both sides don't like the Watchers and view them as fence-sitters. The Watchers are trying to get the clan reunified but they haven't had much success at that, there's just too much blood spilled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T09:58:05-07:00","id":1488042,"title":"","content":"Before Demon the Fallen was published, a brazilian guy created 2 games, &quot;Demon the Price of Power&quot; and &quot;Angel the Salvation&quot;. And of course, depicting an eternal war between Heaven and Hell, with demons and angels hidding from both humanity and the other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> It was a very solid game, he did indeed made a very, very good game with some incredible meta and fluff for it. A pity it is only in portuguese, because I gotta say, it is worth it.<br /> <br /> Now, both demons and angels had powers very similar to Disciplines, albeit a little bit more flexible, and all of them could be easily converted to VtM.<br /> <br /> Now, the reason why Im bringing this up is because I thought of one specific power that he designed for one of the Celestial &quot;Clergy&quot; (like vampiric clans), the Princeps, who are celestial leaders; their power was inspired by the Paladin from Diablo 2, so they have auras of power that can &quot;buff/debuff&quot; enemies.<br /> <br /> This could be a nice change for Valeren for the Salubri warriors.<br /> <br /> There's also a power of healing that would fit the healers all too well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T15:13:37-07:00","id":1488099,"title":"","content":"I'm perfectly fine with the original depiction of the Salubri.<br /> <br /> Vampires who heal or act humanely is not any kind of trope that is needed in a vampire game. An individual vampire who reacts against the horror of being an evil monster that lusts after the blood of the living is fine. You can have various of those. They prop up from time to time in modern vampire literature. But an entire lineage of them is not fulfilling any kind of genre need.<br /> <br /> The only reason they exist is that they serve a specific role in the setting lore - they explain why House Tremere of the Ars Magica game became a vampire clan despite not having the same vampire origins as the other clans. The Salubri were created specifically to be destroyed. That being the case, it was OK for them to be very unvampire-like vampires. It would explain why they were not many of them, or why the other clans quickly agreed to wipe them out - because they never liked them anyway. (Let's face it, while the Tremere started it, they could have never destroyed all the Salubri on their own, the other clans did the vast majority of work on this.) If the Tremere were not in the game, neither would the Salubri be.<br /> <br /> I do have issues with the Dark Ages Salubri because I don't think they were developed in a way that lined up with previous canon. So that would need to be slightly fixed. I'd change the natures of and relations between Saulot's original childer (the Warrior line) and the new childer he created after returning from the East/achieved Golconda (the Healer line). There would not be a &quot;choice&quot; in this matter for characters. You were either embraced by one lineage or the other.<br /> <br /> The original Salubri description implied there was something different about this second batch of Salubri from the first. The second batch all followed Saulot's quest for Golconda, implying the first did not (at least no more than other vampires did), and that when the Tremere purge began this first batch was easier to hunt down and kill because the second batch was &quot;somehow resistant to the order's magics.&quot; So I'd give the first batch (the Warriors) a feeling that their founder considered them to be something of a disappointment, and thus why they were &quot;replaced&quot;. The two lines were still &quot;family&quot;, but more in the case of step-siblings or half-siblings than full siblings. So there was some distrust and resentment of the elder, discarded brother against the younger, favored one. (I think such disunity, perhaps even feud, makes it more plausible that the Salubri could be wiped out).<br /> <br /> I'd also make that Obeah/Healing Valeren only appeared with Saulot's second batch. While anyone could learn that Discipline, that was not the in-clan Discipline of the Warrior line. I'd make Valeren solely the warrior version of Valeren, and it being the in-clan Discipline of that first batch of childer. The two Disciplines are not related except that both sprung from the blood of Saulot. And Valeren does not produce the third eye - that only happens with Obeah.<br /> <br /> I think making it clear that these lines are different, albeit related, increases the plausibility of the theory that Saulot was experimenting with different lines of childer (Warrior, Healer, Baali, Tremere, and possibly yet another, earlier line that perished in the Baali Wars) for some reason if an ST wanted to go with that idea.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea that Golconda somehow transformed Saulot, and thus his new batch of childer is different in some real way from his first batch. That provides enough ambiguity for people to wonder whether it was really <i>Golconda</i> that changed Salubri, or whether it was something <i>else</i> that transformed Saulot which he simply told people was &quot;Golconda&quot;. Again, the ST gets to decide.<br /> <br /> I still don't know how to explain why there is a group of seven surviving Salubri (a magical number) and are all exactly eighth generation. All of whom have the exact same beliefs and act the same. Who state that vampirism is an awful condition that dooms the human soul, but who keep on embracing new people anyway. Whom they force to commit diablerie on them. And that their new childer will then behave exactly the same way they did. These are the only Salubri that survived the purge (sorry Salubri anti-tribu, you don't exist). These survivors clearly come from the Healer line, the second batch of Saulot's childer. But they couldn't have been chosen (or survived) at random. They could not be yet another batch of childer, since Saulot did not embrace them. But they were likely a coterie that Saulot recruited. Perhaps either before he went into voluntary torpor (where he was found by the Tremere) or even during it (since powerful vampires do seem to be somehow &quot;active&quot; mentally during torpor). Perhaps Salubri entered torpor only after he finally found the right Salubri who could fulfill this role. They have a part to play in Saulot's hands - he made sure these were protected well enough to survive the purge - but what that part will be is unknown.<br /> <br /> The original Salubri description implies any PC would be an 8th generation character who has already committed diablerie on their sire and finished their indoctrination. I would have it so that any PCs would be a 9th generation childe who has not yet committed diablerie. They're still in the &quot;testing&quot; phase to determine if they are worthy. That way if they screw up, it's not an end to the magical number of Salubri needed. And if they do screw up, defy their sire, or otherwise rebel, it's just really, really bad luck that the nearest Tremere have found out about them, and the local Prince has ordered a blood hunt....<br /> <br /> (I might, just might, have some other lone Healer Salubri who survived the purge. Maybe a survivor who lucked out by being a member of the Children of Osiris or the Inconnu. Or who lies in deep torpor somewhere. Of course, they would be paranoid as hell because every other Salubri that survived past a date seems to be immediately targeted by their enemies. It's shocking on quickly it happens that they get discovered and killed. And they don't know when the hammer might fall on them, or what is protecting them, or actively targeting their clanmates. This is to just give the STs some other means of introducing Salubri lore or plot if they want. But none of the Warrior line ever survived.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 09-27-2022, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T04:13:08-07:00","id":1488155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1488018#post1488018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would their weakness be, then?<br /> <br /> Personally I find the <i>Antitribu</i> weakness plainly stupid. They could get either of those or something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>In of itself it's fine. It becomes a problem for me because I run with &quot;How you choose to hunt effects what disciplines develop&quot; and, plainly, it's a struggle to develop the other disciplines when you can only abuse people for blood. By my own reckoning, Auspex, Presence and Dominate aren't impossible but they are very difficult, but Obfuscate is impossible. Conversely, the healer caste can never learn Potence, Celerity or obfuscate... but that's my own system and I recognize it as such.<br /> <br /> The extra eye screws with the Masquerade too hard. It might've given the progenitors of the Camarilla reason to allow the Salubri Genoicde, but I don't dig it. .<br /> <br /> <br /> One idea I had today that I think is really, really cool. It's WIP so feel free to offer suggestions.<br /> <br /> Saulubri souls are unstable within the body. Every few decades, they loose 1 die in physical attributes. If reduced to 1 dot of any physicals, they lose health levels instead. wasting away if untreated.<br /> Methods to stabilize things:<br /> -Torpor<br /> -Diablerie<br /> -Sucking away someone's soul with Valeren. This may be the prerequisite for option 4<br /> -Replacing their body: a ritual that has them possess a person they embrace: After this process their empty old body can be Diablerized for generation without the usual consequences. This is the most complete method, and will stave off the wasting for a longer period of time than other methods.<br /> <br /> (The Salubri regains their physical disciplines when they do this, though perhaps not right away. )<br /> <br /> I think this'd be super interesting: you can maintain a high humanity rating to keep your torpor times down, or you could ferry souls at the old folks home and try to keep your mass murder low key, or you can rip and tear through the city and target the unjust, or you could experience a new skin and steal a new life every few decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-27-2022, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T07:49:39-07:00","id":1488170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1488099#post1488099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm perfectly fine with the original depiction of the Salubri.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that and I also think it is fine, at least for most play styles.<br /> <br /> But then this thread was partially born from another where the idea of ditching the Tremere was entertained and the Salubri came up as a substitution as the 13th clan. While it doesn't have to be the case, the idea here really is on making them a big clan, specifically, regardless if one feels or not the need for that.<br /> <br /> Exploring those has advantages for anyone who wants to use them as something more present than the original depiction for whatever reason. But it isn't in any way, I think, an assertion that the original doesn't work by itself, it just doesn't fill the same purpose.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd if they're not a required trope for vampires, with the tweaks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> proposed or something to that effect I think they're still a <i>valid</i> one, for whatever it's worth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1488155#post1488155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I had today that I think is really, really cool. It's WIP so feel free to offer suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>9 out of 10 in the cool factor, but in the current form it would be too slow to come up on most games.<br /> <br /> We may be on track for something, but I'm going to work and can't stop to think on it right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T16:15:42-07:00","id":1488221,"title":"","content":"I like the idea (which I'm almost sure is part of the canon) that the 7 Salubri are just the ones that are under protection of the Ashirra, through the deal they made in the Dark Ages. In a way that they are refugees and prisoners. Just so that there is a material basis for the whole myth of the Seven.<br /> <br /> But yeah, something was going on with the Salubri in the Dark Ages for the other Clans to just have these newcomers go nuts. Either the Clan had something everybody could take something from, or hunting them really gave some great PR, and Saulot was seen as a devilish guy with very little room for interpretation. And yeah, all these cases of Clans being whipped out seem bonkers. Cappadocians and Salubri both. Like hell man, they being less social and influential would only make them harder to reach and track.<br /> <br /> I like the &quot;you need permission to drink&quot; Bane, and hoped it was in V5.<br /> Bloodlines I would left it being only Warriors and Healers.<br /> I would make them really fixed in cults, societies or powerful individuals. Just like the ones protected by the Ashirra. I mean, why would they not accept protection by the Tzimisce, would you through your unlife away simply cuz you felt cringe by some of the most nasty ones?<br /> <br /> And I truly believe the Ventrue, Nosferatu (there is Siamko, a russian nosfie, who really hates the Salubri) or someone else, hating the Clan, or getting something really nice with their destruction. The Tremere must've had help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T17:35:55-07:00","id":1488229,"title":"","content":"There is something else too.<br /> I've wondered if the Tremere didn't make themselves look puny and weak, asking the Salubri for help and sanctuary in the first nights.<br /> After all, they were just pseudovampires with no standing, and little understanding of the Cainite World. So they would get much compassion from the Unicorns. <br /> It would make a lot more sense, and be even more treacherous when they used the knowledge they got against them too. Betraying and diablersing their patrons and helpers, hunting down the rest. And even if Saulot indeed wanted all this to happen, it would've made sense also, and helped a lot in making the Salubri to Tremere transition more swiftly. <br /> <br /> I don't know what Kupala would have got out of all this, so I don't know how to involve it. Well, I have my headcanon about it, but that isn't the point here.<br /> But the Tzimisce... Well, Samiel went there and practically gunked the sucker founder of the Fiends. Going down with a great feat under his belt. This makes me think for the longest time, even if it was all a misunderstanding or not, that Salubri and Tzimisce hated the guts of one another. I mean... if the Fiends were going to be mad about some dude getting caught and tortured, I think they would get a lot more pissed if their Ante was too. Even if just for pride, and no actual love for the thing. <br /> <br /> This makes the whole Salubri, Tremere, Tzimisce and Kupala mess even messier. And that is not counting the Ventrue, Nosferatu and Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T21:54:08-07:00","id":1488242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1488229#post1488229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is something else too.<br /> I've wondered if the Tremere didn't make themselves look puny and weak, asking the Salubri for help and sanctuary in the first nights..</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be expanded to make the Tremere actually Salubri, by a bit tweaking of the Tremre lore<br /> They used a Salubri, not a Tzimisce to bacome vampires<br /> The compassionate salubri accepted them as &quot;half-brothers&quot; and helped them and gave sanctuary in their first nights and even if the secret was out, they were mages who became vampires, the Salubri was High Clan with connections in the Courts and could pull a few favors to save their hides, help them establish chantries...<br /> &quot;Forgive them, Father! They don't know what they are doing.&quot; stlye.<br /> The Salubri honestly could have belived the Tremere knew nothing just conducted experiments on a damned creature and the experiments went horribly wrong, and cursed themselves.<br /> They need every help and they share the blood... they are now Family<br /> The the rest is history, Giovanni-style<br /> The holier than thou three eyed &quot;magicans&quot; were replaced from the inside with the more acceptable two eyed magicians. Medicine and healing was always seen magical thrugh the history, not scientific after all. And the young Camarrila quietly nodded, okay, do it<br /> Of course this would make the whole Salubri Sabbat/anarch like the Cappadocian/Harbringers... or their own like the Hecata. The salubri have enough branch to form a Hecata like &quot;Clan&quot;, even the bittered ones accepting the Baali cousins and soul eater Nkulu Zao making their fall from grace complete<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T08:37:19-07:00","id":1488261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1488242#post1488242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This could be expanded to make the Tremere actually Salubri, by a bit tweaking of the Tremre lore<br /> They used a Salubri, not a Tzimisce to bacome vampires<br /> The compassionate salubri accepted them as &quot;half-brothers&quot; and helped them and gave sanctuary in their first nights and even if the secret was out, they were mages who became vampires, the Salubri was High Clan with connections in the Courts and could pull a few favors to save their hides, help them establish chantries...<br /> &quot;Forgive them, Father! They don't know what they are doing.&quot; stlye.<br /> The Salubri honestly could have belived the Tremere knew nothing just conducted experiments on a damned creature and the experiments went horribly wrong, and cursed themselves.<br /> They need every help and they share the blood... they are now Family<br /> The the rest is history, Giovanni-style<br /> The holier than thou three eyed &quot;magicans&quot; were replaced from the inside with the more acceptable two eyed magicians. Medicine and healing was always seen magical thrugh the history, not scientific after all. And the young Camarrila quietly nodded, okay, do it<br /> Of course this would make the whole Salubri Sabbat/anarch like the Cappadocian/Harbringers... or their own like the Hecata. The salubri have enough branch to form a Hecata like &quot;Clan&quot;, even the bittered ones accepting the Baali cousins and soul eater Nkulu Zao making their fall from grace complete</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be fun hehehe<br /> A reunion of triclops healers, paladins, warlocks and diabolists.<br /> Fun family ther.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T04:08:45-07:00","id":1493814,"title":"","content":"Looking at the Salubri in modern nights, I actually really like the Salubri Antitribu. I'd make them the model for modern Salubri as a whole.<br /> <br /> The Salubri used to be a powerful, noble lineage of warrior-prophets, who defended the innocent and healed the sick. They were respected, loved, and admired.<br /> <br /> And the World of Darkness does not suffer goodness for long.<br /> <br /> Their progenitor was consumed, their bloodline was gutted, their allies were nowhere ro be found, and their members were scattered to the four winds. <br /> Because they were too kind, in a world where cruelty wins.<br /> Because they were too honest, in a world where lies let you survive.<br /> Because they were too brave, in a world where cowards get to feast on the corpses of the brave.<br /> <br /> In modern times, they still stubbornly cling to the past. They give each other names of angels and legendary warriors. They enact rituals and knightings, ceremonies to prove to themselves that their way is good. They clad themselves in the robes of justice.<br /> And it's all lies. A lie they tell themselves to justify what they have become.<br /> Because they are killers now. The most brutal, the most merciless, the most single-minded killers in kindred society. Even the Sabbat keep these monsters at arm's length, out of healthy respect for their destructive culture.<br /> <br /> They say &quot;Don't you understand? We must slay the Tremere to restore our honor,&quot; even as they prepare an IED to bomb a busy city street.<br /> They say &quot;Of course we must slay the Camarilla, they abandoned our brothers for their own selfish ends,&quot; even as they pore over maps provided by the Sabbat.<br /> They say &quot;We have honor, but our enemies do not. We cannot risk injustice winning, and so we must debase ourselves to destroy them,&quot; even as they prepare to ambush an unsuspecting neonate with assault rifles and frag grenades.<br /> <br /> The Salubri are a story of a fall from grace. A microcosm of what happens to good people in a bad world. Where heroes live long enough to become the villains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T05:21:09-07:00","id":1493820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pang4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1493814#post1493814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the Salubri in modern nights, I actually really like the Salubri Antitribu. I'd make them the model for modern Salubri as a whole.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>My biggest issue with the Salubri Antitribu is how did they indoctrinate a bunch of people into becoming fanatical avengers for a fallen Antediluvian in a sect that utterly hates the Antediluvians?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T06:26:52-07:00","id":1493824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487957-remaking-the-salubri?p=1493820#post1493820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My biggest issue with the Salubri Antitribu is how did they indoctrinate a bunch of people into becoming fanatical avengers for a fallen Antediluvian in a sect that utterly hates the Antediluvians?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the _bad_ Antediluvians. Not the good ones, like Saulot and Cappadocius. They're dead, so we can idolize and contort their image however we please.<br /> <br /> I like the inherent hypocrisy and self-deception in their culture, but maybe that was apparent XP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T11:51:43-07:00","id":1494800,"title":"","content":"I'd have the Sabbat Salubri arise somewhat earlier, and reach the level of unofficial warleaders by the modem nights. They're also not fighting to avenge Salout, who cares about someone who couldn't defend himself, so much as the status and rights they think the Tremere stole.<br /> <br /> They had aspirations of joining the Camarilla once, but their weakness made negotiations difficult and when the Tremere were allowed to join many of their elders abandoned the idea entirely. These days there are only a handful of Salubri Antitribu in the Camarilla, the Tremere drove out or killed every one they could.<br /> <br /> Culturally they maintain more of the nobility of their Dark Ages counterparts, but like many knights in reality they range anywhere from saints to thugs. The two castes are mostly a cultural difference, all Salubri have the enforced consensualism weakness and a discipline spread and haven't decided upon, and the Healers are known as the Mystics. They do not regularly practice blood sorcery, but the Salubri Mystics form the Sabbat's premier group of arcane scholars. Not that you'll meet a mystic, they're even rarer than the warriors.<br /> <br /> That's with regards to Europe and America anyway. The rest of the world operates more similarly to canon (although still with the enforced consensualism).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T23:18:20-07:00","id":1494841,"title":"","content":"I have never undertood why there wa a clan of Healers among the Kindred. To me it feels just strange. If I would change this clan. I would change it into a clan of Mystics that sought to find hidden truths about the world and the curse of Caine. Not so much scholars, but instead ascetic mystics who wandered the world in order to find anwers to questions only they seem to ask.<br /> <br /> This was the reason Saulot was embraced by his sire. Saulot was a dedicated mystic who his sire saw as the perfect childe in order to understand the Beast within and the Curse of the Divine God that had placed the curse upon Caine and how to escape it. When the third generation slew the second. Saulot saw this as either as a necessary thing to happen or he was not present.<br /> <br /> During his travels he encountered spiritual seeker both those of the martial bend, holy healers, seekers of the question of &quot;why do we exist as humans&quot; and formed a small cultish group of ghouls and kindred. It was on these journeys that he found out about Golconda.<br /> <br /> So Saulot was more a blend of a Christian Gnostic from the first centuries after the formation of the Christian faith, a hindu/Buddhist monk (and if you know Ars Magica, a Criamon).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}